# ABOUTME: Template .envrc for Proton Pass per-project secrets (API-credential items).
# ABOUTME: Easiest path: `proton-envrc <context> >> .envrc` then `direnv allow`.
#
# Convention (Proton "API Credential" item): the item's "API Key" field is the env var
# NAME, the "Secret" field is the value. Reference the value with /Secret.
# Contexts map to per-context vaults; list them: ls ~/.claude/channels/proton-pass/*.pat

# Bind this folder to ONE context/vault. A jailbroken agent here can only authenticate
# as this context, so it reads only this vault.

# They look like (id-based refs are robust against spaced titles):
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY='pass://<share-id>/<item-id>/Secret'   # Anthropic

use proton money resolve

# Generate the export lines + trailing use-proton line automatically (recommended):
#   proton-envrc money --resolve >> .envrc     # project repo (values resolved into env)
#   proton-envrc money >> .envrc               # capability repo (refs stay refs)
# In a capability repo, run tools through:  secrets run -- <cmd>
